✅ LinkedIn Post:- SOC Role (Blue Team) – TryHackMe Lab

🚀 Completed the “SOC Role – Blue Team” lab on TryHackMe!:-
 
This room gave me a solid understanding of how Security Operations Centers (SOC) work and what responsibilities a Junior Security Analyst handles on a daily basis.

🔍 🔹 Lab Overview:-

The TryHackMe SOC Role room introduces core blue-team concepts and explains how SOC teams detect, analyze, and respond to cyber threats.
 I explored how different SOC tiers operate, what tools analysts use, and how incidents flow through the SOC.

🛡️ 🔹 My Learnings from the Lab:-

1️⃣ Understanding SOC Structure:-

Tier 1 (L1) – Monitors alerts, triages, escalates incidents
Tier 2 (L2) – Deep investigation, malware analysis, threat hunting
Tier 3 (L3) – Advanced forensics, creating detection rules, tuning SIEM
SOC Manager – Oversees SOC operations & incident lifecycle

2️⃣ Daily Responsibilities of a SOC Analyst:-

Monitoring SIEM alerts
Investigating suspicious IPs, domains, and user actions
Writing incident reports
Performing log correlation
Blocking malicious activity
Supporting incident response

3️⃣ Tools Covered:-

SIEM (Security Information and Event Management)
 Used to collect, search, and analyze logs
EDR/XDR for endpoint detection
Threat Intelligence Platforms
Firewall/IDS dashboards

4️⃣ How an Incident Flows in a SOC:-

Alert Triggered →
L1 Verifies the alert →
Escalation to L2 if suspicious →
L2 detailed investigation →
Containment & remediation →
Reporting & closing the ticket

📘 🔹 Why This Lab is Valuable:-

This room strengthened my understanding of:
How blue teams actually work in real organizations
The lifecycle of security alerts
How SOC analysts detect and stop real-world threats
Industry-level workflows & documentation practices

🧠 Key Takeaways:-

✔ SOC is the backbone of enterprise security
 ✔ Incident analysis needs attention to detail
 ✔ SIEM triage is a core skill for blue-teamers
 ✔ Threat intelligence is crucial for decision-making
 ✔ Communication & reporting are as important as technical skills

🏁 Proud to Level Up My Blue-Team Skills!:-

This lab gave me hands-on knowledge that aligns with real SOC duties — great for anyone preparing for SOC Analyst, Blue Team, or Cybersecurity Analyst roles.
